Description: Fast on-device "Read Aloud" text-to-speech (sanoTTS heart voices)
 A small Wayland "Read Aloud" window: highlight text in any app, click READ, and
 it is spoken through your default audio output. It uses the native audio.cpp
 sanoTTS engine with the "heart" voice (and the smaller, faster "heart-nano"),
 which run many times faster than real time on a Raspberry Pi 4 / 400, so speech
 starts almost immediately. The DSP is tuned for clarity (gain, noise gate,
 consonant lift, loudness leveler).
 .
 Playback goes through PipeWire (pw-play) so it follows your current output and
 mixes with other audio, falling back to ALSA. Also provides a command-line
 "heart-say" for speaking text or the clipboard from a terminal, and
 "heart-tts-doctor" to check the install. The voice models are bundled.
